# L §2.5: "At a position keyed by a stepped range (§5.6), a key is a value of the range's type, written or computed,
# and must be one of the range's values, a + i·s ≤ b for a whole number i ≥ 0 (LOAD-KEY for a literal, RUN-KEY at
# run)." dbl is keyed by 0 .. ci (ci = 10): the written key 4 gives 4 + 4 = 8; the computed key x2 = 12 is outside:
# RUN-KEY. (Writer 6: the written key was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §2.5, and no read checked the range.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input ci: int
input x2: int

def dbl[g in 0 .. ci]: int = g + g

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  ci = 10 "s"
  x2 = 12 "s"

ask q3: dbl[4]
ask q6: dbl[x2]
=== expect
q3: 8
  cut 2026-12-31
q6: refused: RUN-KEY 12 is not a value of 0 .. 10
  cut 2026-12-31
